From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vpss: an end of frame without an input is not an error

The server unbinds VI from VPSS and disables the channel when it parks the
outputs without viewers (20 s after each boot, and after the last viewer
leaves) and when it hands an output to VI-direct capture. An end of frame
that comes after that finds no input frame in the work queue, and
vpss_handle_frame_done() logged two kernel errors, "No more vb for dequeue"
and "can't get vb-blk". There is nothing to give back then: the dequeue
only failed. Say it at debug level and skip it; nothing else changes.
---
--- a/interdrv/vpss/common/vpss.c
+++ b/interdrv/vpss/common/vpss.c
@@ -2952,11 +2952,21 @@
 
 	vpssExtCtx[workingGrp].grp_state = GRP_STATE_IDLE;
 
-	vb_dqbuf(chn, CHN_TYPE_IN, &blk);
-	if (blk == VB_INVALID_HANDLE) {
-		CVI_TRACE_VPSS(CVI_DBG_ERR, "Mod(%d) can't get vb-blk.\n", chn.enModId);
+	/*
+	 * An end of frame can come after the input stopped: NanoKVM unbinds VI
+	 * and disables the channel when it parks the outputs without viewers or
+	 * hands an output to VI-direct capture. There is no input frame to give
+	 * back then, and dequeuing would only fail; that is not an error.
+	 */
+	if (base_mod_jobs_workq_empty(chn, CHN_TYPE_IN)) {
+		CVI_TRACE_VPSS(CVI_DBG_DEBUG, "Grp(%d) end of frame without an input\n", workingGrp);
 	} else {
-		vb_done_handler(chn, CHN_TYPE_IN, blk);
+		vb_dqbuf(chn, CHN_TYPE_IN, &blk);
+		if (blk == VB_INVALID_HANDLE) {
+			CVI_TRACE_VPSS(CVI_DBG_ERR, "Mod(%d) can't get vb-blk.\n", chn.enModId);
+		} else {
+			vb_done_handler(chn, CHN_TYPE_IN, blk);
+		}
 	}
 
 	VpssChn = 0;
